0811DEE0 modifier-table-destroy-return

The task scheduler supplies the retiring table owner in r0. The
table is created only when gScriptRecordTable is null, and its
initializer publishes that same owner. ROM probes on checkpoint
0028 show the destroy argument equals the published table pointer.

The explicit form changed the ROM bytes. The guarded form passed the unit ROM check.

--- a/src/script/script_options.c
+++ b/src/script/script_options.c
@@ -174,5 +174,11 @@
 u32 Modifier_OnTableTaskDestroy(void)
 {
+#ifdef UBFIX
+    u32 owner = (u32)gScriptRecordTable;
+#endif
     gScriptRecordTable = 0;
+#ifdef UBFIX
+    return owner;
+#endif
 }
 
